@node Standard Libraries
@appendix Standard Libraries

This section lists the exports provided by the standard libraries.  The
libraries are factored so as to separate features which might not be
sup@value{shy}ported by all implementations, or which might be expensive
to load.

The @code{scheme} library prefix is used for all standard libraries, and
is reserved for use by future standards.

@node Base Library
@appendixsec Base Library

The @code{(scheme base)} library exports many of the procedures and
syntax bind@value{shy}ings that are traditionally associated with
Scheme.  The division between the base library and the other standard
libraries is based on use, not on con@value{shy}struc@value{shy}tion.
In particular, some facilities that are typically implemented as
primitives by a compiler or the run-time system rather than in terms of
other standard procedures or syntax are not part of the base library,
but are defined in separate libraries.  By the same token, some exports
of the base library are implementable in terms of other exports.  They
are redundant in the strict sense of the word, but they capture common
patterns of usage, and are therefore provided as convenient
abbreviations.

